WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:03.937
Legend has it...

00:05.106 --> 00:07.904
...that during the Heian Period, there
were men who fought with no weapons...

00:08.243 --> 00:13.579
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:15.050 --> 00:20.215
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.335 --> 00:40.764
<i>The Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:41.042 --> 00:46.878
<i>Rushing through my innocent
youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.416 --> 00:54.321
<i>This soul of mine is
so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.990 --> 00:59.756
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.861 --> 01:03.024
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.835 --> 01:13.900
<i>This is what I'm wishing
for as I sing this song.</i>

01:14.075 --> 01:19.911
<i>I want you to acknowledge
me, that's all.</i>

01:20.782 --> 01:28.052
<i>You smiled at me for
the very first time.</i>

01:28.223 --> 01:36.597
<i>Thank you so much, thank you
from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.298 --> 01:38.993
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.743 --> 01:52.179
<i>The Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

02:12.801 --> 02:14.792
What a waste!

02:16.805 --> 02:19.069
Who the hell are you?

02:19.174 --> 02:20.869
You mean my name?

02:21.309 --> 02:22.833
Just call me Takato.

02:28.783 --> 02:29.943
What the...

02:30.185 --> 02:31.413
What are you looking at?

02:31.519 --> 02:32.918
Oh, and by the way...

02:33.054 --> 02:35.921
I guess you could say I'm on your side...

02:36.157 --> 02:36.885
What!

02:36.991 --> 02:38.458
You have a past, don't you?

03:04.018 --> 03:09.923
<i>A MAN OF NO SCRUPLES</i>

03:38.686 --> 03:39.516
Hey...

03:41.322 --> 03:42.482
That rice ball is mine!

03:43.491 --> 03:45.721
But you've still got
another one in your hand...

03:46.127 --> 03:48.493
Shut up. You've already had six of them!

03:48.630 --> 03:50.530
I'm still only on my fourth...

03:50.965 --> 03:52.296
So what if you are?

03:52.400 --> 03:55.528
You're a lot smaller than I am, so
why shouldn't you be eating less?

03:55.803 --> 03:56.861
Don't give me that.

03:56.971 --> 03:59.667
Anyway, Sasuke was the one
who got us these rice balls!

04:00.074 --> 04:04.101
Hey, after wolfing down that boar
I caught, who are you to talk?

04:12.020 --> 04:14.853
If you really want it, defeat
me first. Then you can take it!

04:15.323 --> 04:18.315
I'm letting you tag along because
Sasuke seems to think it's a good idea...

04:18.459 --> 04:21.019
...but that doesn't mean
you and I are friends!

04:23.398 --> 04:25.161
Draw your weapon!

04:25.333 --> 04:28.632
I'm going to show you right now
that I can get along just fine...

04:29.003 --> 04:30.493
...without you as my "ally"!

04:32.206 --> 04:33.673
Oh well...

04:34.642 --> 04:35.939
I'm tough to beat, you know...

04:36.511 --> 04:38.103
Right, I'm sure you are...

04:38.446 --> 04:40.710
...but, not as tough as I am!

04:43.718 --> 04:44.912
Come on, get up!

04:45.286 --> 04:46.776
Are we really gonna do this?

04:46.921 --> 04:47.478
That's right!

04:48.122 --> 04:49.453
This rice ball is MINE!

04:50.091 --> 04:51.251
No matter what?

04:57.031 --> 04:58.760
Please, stop!

05:12.113 --> 05:13.273
Sasuke!

05:13.881 --> 05:14.711
Hey...

05:14.949 --> 05:17.713
Forget these trivial matters...

05:17.986 --> 05:20.614
No rice ball of mine
is a trivial matter!

05:20.722 --> 05:21.916
Of course not...

05:22.056 --> 05:26.925
...but listen, Hyogonosuke Toshitoshi
of the Owari Yagyu clan has arrived.

05:27.462 --> 05:30.727
If we go back the way we
came, there is a tea-house...

05:31.232 --> 05:33.996
Good, then that's where we'll
lie in wait to ambush him!

05:34.102 --> 05:37.265
First Iori Miyamoto, and
now the famous Owari Yagyu?

05:38.039 --> 05:39.939
What in the hell are you guys up to?

05:40.041 --> 05:40.973
Just shut up, you moron!

05:41.576 --> 05:43.271
Let's go, Sasuke!

05:47.181 --> 05:48.170
Mr. Takato...

05:49.384 --> 05:51.375
Hey, I'm on your side!

06:01.562 --> 06:03.359
Hmm, so he's not here yet...

06:04.065 --> 06:06.659
Right then, I'll wait in the tea-house.

06:06.768 --> 06:09.236
Sasuke, you stay in the shadows
and fend off the retainers.

06:09.604 --> 06:11.231
Young Miss, wait a moment.

06:11.706 --> 06:13.333
What's the matter, Sasuke?

06:18.012 --> 06:21.413
I sense a threatening
presence in that tea-house...

06:21.749 --> 06:23.580
Who is he?

06:32.026 --> 06:35.052
It doesn't matter who,
that man's kenki...

06:35.129 --> 06:36.061
You're right...

06:36.130 --> 06:38.189
...it's as powerful as
an unsheathed blade...

06:38.800 --> 06:41.200
I've never known anyone
with kenki like this...

06:41.302 --> 06:42.166
It can't be...

06:42.503 --> 06:43.629
...Musashi Miyamoto!

06:44.105 --> 06:48.804
Compared to Musashi in his younger
days, this man is far more tranquil...

06:49.544 --> 06:51.978
...but I can sense there's
something more to him...

06:52.380 --> 06:56.476
I thought Musashi was sending
Iori to compete in his place?

06:56.617 --> 06:58.949
Here comes Owari Yagyu...

07:19.373 --> 07:20.670
Who the hell are you?

07:20.775 --> 07:22.265
Can't you see you're blocking the road?

07:22.744 --> 07:23.733
Are they going to fight?

07:24.278 --> 07:25.245
Father...

07:26.881 --> 07:31.147
You never could suppress that
kenki of yours, could you, Jubei?

07:32.019 --> 07:33.043
Jubei?

07:33.421 --> 07:35.787
So that's the Edo
Yagyu's No. 1 swordsman...

07:35.890 --> 07:36.447
Really?

07:36.791 --> 07:40.318
I, Sasuke, have seen many
a swordsman in my lifetime...

07:40.495 --> 07:43.623
...but this is the first time
that I've ever seen anyone...

07:43.698 --> 07:45.632
...with the same kind of
kenki as Musashi Miyamoto.

07:45.700 --> 07:49.227
Not even his adopted son Iori
possesses it to that degree...

07:49.337 --> 07:51.999
A man who emanates
the same ki as Musashi...

07:52.340 --> 07:53.705
...Jubei Yagyu!

07:54.008 --> 07:58.001
If I didn't know you better, I'd think
you were challenging me to a duel!

07:58.312 --> 08:02.476
Unfortunately, it is part of my
nature, and I'm unable to control it.

08:02.884 --> 08:05.614
So, was it an accident
that we crossed paths here?

08:05.720 --> 08:07.085
Or is it...

08:07.221 --> 08:09.246
Let's just say it was
partly by chance...

08:09.357 --> 08:12.588
A little probing before
the tournament, eh?

08:12.894 --> 08:16.159
Unfortunately, I doubt
that I will be competing.

08:16.597 --> 08:20.397
But I thought you were on your
way to Edo for that very purpose?

08:20.735 --> 08:23.431
I heard Musashi won't be competing...

08:23.538 --> 08:25.096
That is what changed my mind.

08:25.506 --> 08:29.203
I see, so you don't find
me worth your while...

08:29.677 --> 08:31.008
If I may be so bold, sir...

08:31.112 --> 08:35.981
...my father Munenori is the one who
should face you in the tournament.

08:36.117 --> 08:36.913
How dare you!

08:37.018 --> 08:39.748
Why should my father
deign to take you on?

08:39.954 --> 08:41.319
I'll defeat you myself!

08:59.140 --> 09:00.937
Stand back, Mozaemon.

09:04.278 --> 09:07.372
Please forgive the boy for
losing control, however...

09:07.815 --> 09:09.248
That man...

09:09.350 --> 09:11.580
Had he drawn his sword
he'd be dead now...

09:12.954 --> 09:16.515
Unlike your father, I still
have a few more duels left in me.

09:17.058 --> 09:19.652
But I will not be compared
to a man who would...

09:19.794 --> 09:22.160
...exchange his sword
for political gain!

09:22.363 --> 09:23.955
I couldn't agree with you more...

09:24.265 --> 09:28.702
If you don't compete, then it will
be the end of the Edo Yagyu Branch.

09:28.803 --> 09:31.567
We shall be on our way.
But Jubei, what will you do?

09:32.607 --> 09:33.403
Well, then...

09:35.142 --> 09:36.575
He knows we're here!

09:36.978 --> 09:38.707
I think I'd have more fun...

09:38.946 --> 09:42.211
...taking on those three in the
bushes than going to the tournament.

09:42.583 --> 09:43.641
However...

09:44.118 --> 09:46.985
Since we've met, I think I
will accompany you to Edo.

09:47.088 --> 09:47.520
Good.

09:48.389 --> 09:49.720
Oh no, he's leaving!

09:50.324 --> 09:51.655
Let go of me, Sasuke!

09:53.394 --> 09:56.192
It's no use, Young Miss.

10:04.705 --> 10:06.070
Why did you stop me?

10:06.173 --> 10:08.698
It would be sheer recklessness
to try and take on...

10:08.843 --> 10:10.435
...both Jubei and the
head of the Owari Yagyu.

10:10.544 --> 10:13.104
It's better to go to Edo, and
lay out our strategy there...

10:14.715 --> 10:16.114
Jubei, huh?

10:23.157 --> 10:28.094
Still, Edo has come a long way in a
short time, has it not, Young Miss?

10:29.964 --> 10:30.692
Ouch!

10:32.600 --> 10:35.865
It won't be ready for a few
minutes yet, so please be patient.

10:36.003 --> 10:37.834
What a little glutton!

10:38.139 --> 10:39.265
Whoa!

10:40.174 --> 10:42.802
So who's your next target, anyway?

10:43.010 --> 10:44.910
I thought at first you
two were out for revenge...

10:45.012 --> 10:46.980
...but it doesn't really
look that way now...

10:47.181 --> 10:51.447
You don't care who you fight, as
long as he's a renowned swordsman.

10:51.953 --> 10:54.217
Don't tell me your plot
is to defeat all these...

10:54.322 --> 10:56.950
...master swordsmen to claim a
spot in the Shogun's Tournament?

10:57.625 --> 10:58.649
Ow! Hot! Hot!

10:58.793 --> 11:00.351
Bull's eye, huh?

11:00.594 --> 11:02.323
You need to learn to
conceal your feelings!

11:02.563 --> 11:03.325
Huh?

11:03.464 --> 11:06.262
Well, well... your perception is dead-on.

11:06.367 --> 11:07.265
Sasuke!

11:07.668 --> 11:10.569
It is true, when we heard
about the Shogun's Tournament...

11:10.771 --> 11:13.604
...we thought we could earn
the chance to compete...

11:13.708 --> 11:18.077
...if we defeated a number of master
swordsmen under the Mutsu name.

11:18.512 --> 11:20.537
Is the Mutsu name really worth assuming?

11:20.681 --> 11:24.208
Certainly, it is a name
celebrated in legend.

11:25.553 --> 11:27.180
No one knows for sure...

11:27.321 --> 11:30.757
...but they say that even the great
Musashi was defeated by a Mutsu...

11:54.048 --> 11:58.576
I decided that our best chance
lay in using this particular name.

11:59.053 --> 12:00.543
So what's in it for you?

12:01.055 --> 12:06.322
No ninja would go to all this trouble
just to compete in front of the Shogun.

12:06.527 --> 12:10.588
What we're after is the
Shogun Iemitsu's head.

12:11.032 --> 12:12.329
Just shut up, Sasuke!

12:13.134 --> 12:14.965
I never would've guessed!

12:15.236 --> 12:17.932
But that's right, you are
the last of the Sanadas.

12:18.973 --> 12:21.874
She is Lord Yukimura's posthumous child.

12:21.976 --> 12:23.671
That's what you say, Sasuke.

12:24.311 --> 12:25.835
It was 19 years ago...

12:26.147 --> 12:29.275
My lord and master,
Lord Yukimura Sanada...

12:29.583 --> 12:32.416
...even as Osaka was about to fall...

12:32.586 --> 12:36.022
...he was the only warrior on the
Toyotomi side able to strike terror...

12:36.123 --> 12:38.148
...into Ieyasu's heart.

12:38.793 --> 12:42.729
Leading only 3,500 men
against 15,000 Tokugawa troops...

12:42.863 --> 12:47.232
...he attacked again and again,
until finally he was within...

12:47.401 --> 12:49.892
...striking distance of Ieyasu himself.

12:50.037 --> 12:51.937
But as he was hopelessly outnumbered...

12:52.506 --> 12:57.239
...my lord eventually met
his death on the battlefield.

12:58.312 --> 13:00.837
Just before his final moments...

13:06.520 --> 13:08.112
Where is Sasuke?

13:08.322 --> 13:09.846
Sir, here I am.

13:10.357 --> 13:13.485
You should be commended
for having served such a...

13:13.594 --> 13:15.653
...foolhardy master all these years.

13:15.796 --> 13:18.822
I, Saemon-no-suke,
have no words of thanks.

13:19.100 --> 13:20.567
What a thing to say, my Lord.

13:20.701 --> 13:22.931
You are the finest samurai in the land.

13:23.537 --> 13:26.097
But if I hadn't chosen to
fight for the Toyotomi Clan...

13:26.240 --> 13:28.265
...knowing they were going to lose...

13:28.375 --> 13:32.209
...then I wouldn't have had to send
so many of my men to their deaths.

13:33.781 --> 13:34.873
Even so...

13:34.982 --> 13:38.543
They claimed that the inscription
on the bell cast by Lord Hideyori...

13:38.953 --> 13:41.478
...contained a jinx on the Tokugawas.

13:41.622 --> 13:46.184
Using such an outrageous pretext
for destroying the Toyotomi Clan!

13:46.327 --> 13:47.589
I could not forgive Ieyasu!

13:48.329 --> 13:51.856
I thought my strategy would let me
rise up against the arrogant leyasu...

13:52.166 --> 13:55.135
...and catch him by surprise!

13:55.903 --> 13:58.303
Rather than remaining a minor daimyo...

13:58.506 --> 14:01.907
...I wanted to become
a legend in my own time...

14:02.676 --> 14:08.137
But I am only a fool trying
to resist the winds of change.

14:08.849 --> 14:12.546
All I can do now is lead all
my men into certain death.

14:13.053 --> 14:17.080
We desire nothing more than
to accompany you in death!

14:17.525 --> 14:18.549
Sasuke!

14:19.360 --> 14:20.850
It is not time for you to die...

14:21.195 --> 14:21.820
My Lord?

14:23.063 --> 14:26.794
I want you to look after Nae,
whom I've left behind in Osaka.

14:27.368 --> 14:31.236
She is only seventeen, I
cannot bear to let her die.

14:32.072 --> 14:35.405
Especially since she
is carrying my child...

14:37.611 --> 14:39.272
Take this sword...

14:40.247 --> 14:41.509
...my Muramasa...

14:41.649 --> 14:44.709
If my child is born, then
this sword shall protect him.

14:44.818 --> 14:45.614
My lord!

14:45.986 --> 14:48.420
Are you asking me, my Lord...

14:49.156 --> 14:52.853
Forgive me, Sasuke, there
is no one else I can ask.

14:56.497 --> 14:57.486
Men!

14:58.365 --> 15:00.356
Before we fall...

15:00.534 --> 15:04.300
...we shall make sure Ieyasu never
forgets the sight of the Sanada banner!

15:04.438 --> 15:06.963
My Lord!

15:10.010 --> 15:10.977
My Lord!

15:11.545 --> 15:14.105
My Lord!

15:15.149 --> 15:19.051
Six months later, my lady Nae
gave birth to a daughter...

15:19.153 --> 15:20.814
...and that was Miss Tsubura.

15:20.921 --> 15:25.017
Sadly, though, my lady Nae never recovered
from the shock of my lord's death.

15:25.626 --> 15:27.821
My lady passed away
soon after giving birth.

15:27.962 --> 15:30.021
And so it was I who raised the child.

15:30.164 --> 15:33.224
So that thing you're carrying,
that's his Muramasa, huh?

15:33.534 --> 15:36.697
They say that the Tokugawas
are cursed by Muramasa swords...

15:36.870 --> 15:38.303
...isn't that right?

15:39.240 --> 15:43.802
Leaving that Muramasa to you was
a command to destroy the Tokugawas...

15:43.911 --> 15:45.776
...is that what you're saying he meant?

15:45.946 --> 15:48.642
Well, on that point I cannot be sure.

15:48.983 --> 15:52.111
My lord said it was
to protect his child...

15:52.286 --> 15:54.117
Those were his words, nothing more.

15:54.255 --> 15:56.348
Of course he meant
for us to get revenge!

15:56.490 --> 15:58.856
But what good would
it do to kill Iemitsu?

15:59.293 --> 16:03.024
The only thing it might do is
bring back nationwide chaos.

16:03.264 --> 16:06.825
Why start all that bloodshed again
after we've finally put that behind us?

16:07.468 --> 16:10.062
The Toyotomi Clan had
already established peace.

16:10.204 --> 16:12.672
It was the Tokugawas
who brought on war again!

16:12.806 --> 16:16.264
Listen, I know where
you're coming from, but...

16:16.510 --> 16:18.205
Sasuke! Kill this moron!

16:18.345 --> 16:20.313
Now that he's heard everything
we can't let him live!

16:21.348 --> 16:22.280
Wanna fight?

16:22.950 --> 16:23.882
Mr. Takato!

16:24.084 --> 16:26.314
I, Sasuke, am imploring you.

16:26.420 --> 16:27.819
Please stay with us as our ally!

16:28.255 --> 16:29.984
The Young Miss may speak harshly to you...

16:30.090 --> 16:33.184
...but by no means does
she bear you any ill will!

16:33.827 --> 16:35.158
Sasuke...

16:36.297 --> 16:37.958
Well, what can I do?

16:38.399 --> 16:40.162
All right, fine, but
let's eat now, okay?

16:40.467 --> 16:43.595
I'm starving, so we'll talk afterwards.

16:43.737 --> 16:44.499
Hey, dammit!

16:44.638 --> 16:45.832
Don't be such a hog!

16:45.939 --> 16:47.201
There won't be enough for me!

16:47.308 --> 16:48.707
Sasuke, stop him!

16:48.842 --> 16:52.300
Don't bite my head off, there's
still a lot left in the pot.

16:59.720 --> 17:02.211
Now I'm full.

17:04.224 --> 17:05.885
Where you going?

17:06.260 --> 17:07.090
Hey!

17:07.161 --> 17:08.219
Shut up!

17:08.829 --> 17:10.729
Better not follow me or I'll kill you!

17:10.831 --> 17:12.355
Oh, you're gonna pee.

17:20.107 --> 17:22.769
I'm supposed to be your ally, remember?

17:23.077 --> 17:24.942
Give me a break!

17:25.079 --> 17:29.038
If you take one step over that line,
the next one will find its mark!

17:30.084 --> 17:30.948
Dammit!

17:31.452 --> 17:35.752
At last, the bashful young girl
in Miss Tsubura has emerged.

17:35.856 --> 17:40.418
However, the way she throws
isn't ladylike at all.

17:40.694 --> 17:42.719
Going back to that Muramasa...

17:43.097 --> 17:48.694
I do not believe my lord left her
the sword for the purpose of revenge.

17:48.869 --> 17:52.464
Then why did you raise her
as if she were a female ninja?

17:52.639 --> 17:56.405
Only because I know
nothing beyond ninja skills.

17:56.643 --> 18:00.409
At first, I only meant to teach her
self-defence, but she was so gifted...

18:00.647 --> 18:04.743
...such a natural that she
soon outgrew those tactics.

18:04.885 --> 18:09.345
So I got carried away, and
began training her in earnest...

18:09.490 --> 18:13.392
...until she was skilled
enough to assume the Mutsu name.

18:15.195 --> 18:19.564
So killing Iemitsu means nothing
to me, one way or the other.

18:19.733 --> 18:24.329
It's just as you said, it is
better to live an ordinary life.

18:24.805 --> 18:25.794
You're lying.

18:26.440 --> 18:27.338
Lying?

18:27.708 --> 18:29.539
You mean you don't believe me?

18:29.676 --> 18:34.272
It pains you so much that you
weren't able to die with Yukimura?

18:35.382 --> 18:39.944
Nothing's wrong with living in peace,
nothing's wrong with dying for your beliefs.

18:40.120 --> 18:42.554
That's how I look at it, but...

18:42.990 --> 18:46.926
...don't do it if there's
someone to grieve for you.

18:50.831 --> 18:52.389
I thought I told him not to...

18:52.499 --> 18:53.363
That moron!

18:56.970 --> 18:58.631
No, wait! What the hell?

18:59.006 --> 19:01.065
There's five, no, eight of them...

19:01.742 --> 19:02.868
Maybe more!

19:10.150 --> 19:11.082
Just two...

19:11.285 --> 19:12.980
I shouldn't have used so many before!

19:20.894 --> 19:22.259
Where are they coming from?

19:22.763 --> 19:23.525
Above!

19:47.154 --> 19:47.916
There's too many of them!

20:01.235 --> 20:02.532
A two-tiered system...

20:03.570 --> 20:04.798
I've got you!

20:10.377 --> 20:12.709
I'm impressed by your disappearing act...

20:12.846 --> 20:15.872
...but don't count on beating me
just because my arms are chained.

20:16.283 --> 20:18.114
You are strong...

20:18.318 --> 20:23.085
...but you shouldn't make any fancy
kicks under the present circumstances.

20:25.058 --> 20:25.922
Do it now!

20:31.031 --> 20:33.090
They've got me!

20:35.369 --> 20:36.393
Mr. Takato!

20:36.537 --> 20:37.367
Right.

20:43.210 --> 20:44.142
Young Miss!

20:44.244 --> 20:45.871
They caught us off guard.

20:46.046 --> 20:47.013
Was it the Yagyus?

20:47.114 --> 20:50.641
Probably the Ura-Yagyus
who ambushed Iori!

20:50.951 --> 20:53.818
We let him go so he would spread
the word about the Mutsu legend...

20:54.187 --> 20:56.519
...this is the greatest
mistake of my life!

20:58.325 --> 21:00.225
Mr. Takato, where are you going?

21:01.461 --> 21:02.928
Yagyu...

21:04.298 --> 21:06.425
To the Yagyu mansion!

21:13.907 --> 21:16.243
I suppose I'll have to face off with him!

21:16.243 --> 21:18.879
<i>I suppose I'll have to face off with him!
To be continued...</i>

21:18.879 --> 21:21.211
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:32.326 --> 21:44.397
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at
them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.671 --> 21:54.410
<i>My loneliness and the vast night
sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:54.548 --> 22:03.547
<i>I just don't know what this
dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.690 --> 22:14.362
<i>Even if it's just hello,
I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:15.402 --> 22:21.534
<i>The person I am today
is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.908 --> 22:24.900
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.779 --> 22:32.048
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:32.352 --> 22:37.847
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.472 --> 22:54.337
Takato and Sasuke have infiltrated the...

22:54.474 --> 22:57.238
...Yagyu residence in search
of the captured Tsubura.

22:57.377 --> 23:00.073
But lying in wait for them is...

23:00.947 --> 23:02.414
Next episode of Age of Chaos...

23:02.549 --> 23:04.380
<i>THE MUTSU CONSPIRACY</i>

23:04.484 --> 23:06.645
Pay close attention, and wait!
